mini-swe-agent (step 7, $0.01):
The function OllamaChatWrapper.format collects messages, combines system 
messages and conversation history into a single "system" role message. This is 
different from the docstring which says that user messages should have the 
"user" role.

The implementation creates a system message with all the content (including 
conversation history and previous messages) and returns it with the role 
"system". There is no separation of roles as "user" or "assistant" in the 
returned messages.

To fix the issue, we should change the implementation so that the function 
outputs user messages with the role "user" as the docstring describes, not 
bundle everything into a single system message.

I will now modify the function implementation to align with the docstring, 
fixing the role assignments in the output messages.

